Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s come up with some sort of a model. So let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s say that we learn a concept of a set and and say that it \
is a collection of objects. Then we can represent this in some sort of a \
graph with node labelled ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["Set", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4743727a-cf0c-431d-9760-ce5498f723f7"],
 " and it being a collection of objects. So it is linked with the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]idea\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of a collection of \
objects perhaps by undirected edges. Then we have the directed edges to \
examples such as the naturals etc. For instance, something like this:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.969459071425818*^9, {3.969504678917193*^9, 3.969504679404353*^9}, {
   3.969611993235515*^9, 
   3.969611995297682*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8250fd6d-b1ce-40a4-9eff-\
9eab12d053c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reality",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": It is probably better to start reading literature and seeing how Lean \
Dojo and other things work."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96961199658048*^9, 3.969612002030406*^9}, {
