Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s just ask what are the parameters of our model? the \
degrees of freedom which want to make the predictions. so let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s come up with this. Basically, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", " ", ":", " ", "input"}], " ", "->", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", 
     SubscriptBox["n", "1"]]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aa388a23-e853-4a30-8bce-a2e3be11e2a8"],
 " is the first layer. Then,  maps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"  ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", 
      SubscriptBox["n", "1"]], " ", "->", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["n", "2"], " "}]], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", 
        SubscriptBox["n", "3"]], "->", " ", "..."}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"8580af75-4f80-48a1-af44-44f9aa4d43c6"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["n", "1"], " ", ">", 
    SubscriptBox["n", "2"], ">", 
    SubscriptBox["n", "3"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2ba040cc-3ebb-4d71-a49f-f40d42948208"],
 " are successive things, which are somewhat random functions in a sense \
representing a random walk with probably more and more attention and \
stability (ooh ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "650735f8-3a6a-4b31-be49-4c1e205d8872"],
 " I like that idea). Thus, if the input is \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]a set is a \
collection of objects\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], then the representation can be \
like that. "
}], "Item",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968925057353464*^9, 3.968925075433436*^9}, {
   3.96892550260637*^9, 3.968925554223379*^9}, {3.968925631851144*^9, 
