Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The transition from the input to the output is actually some sort of a \
physical process. So somthing is literally happening. If I\[CloseCurlyQuote]m \
giving it an input..it has to take it in. but we can simulate that process \
somehow n a nice way. Thus, if the input text is something like \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]a set is a collection of objects\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], then the output is some thing in the layers of the \
agent. And those things are related to other layers in the agent. So we are \
just asking about the representation of knowledge. that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
really it. we agreed to do it in english language. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
forget about the brain. "
}], "Item",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968925057353464*^9, 3.968925075433436*^9}, {
