Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The only problem that seemingly exists is that the possible inputs is an \
infinite set, and having a node for each of them is impossible. The way \
ChatGPT deals with this is that it accepts the set of tokens i.e. the \
building blocks of the language are finite. Then, if a sentence is input, we \
can convert that into another number and thus the only function is some \
function from the reals to the reals. "
}], "Item",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968925057353464*^9, 3.968925075433436*^9}, {
