Cell["\<\
However, it seems that the brain doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t work like that. \
when i read something i haven\[CloseCurlyQuote]t read, it gives me some weird \
feelings related to something i have felt before. when i read perturbation \
methods, it gave me some image of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]vibrations\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and/or something like that. Hmm. It just seems weird \
to have a thing called \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]perturbation\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as a node. There\[CloseCurlyQuote]s also the \
question of taking things in context of one another. weird. man. let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s read that sensory input paper.\
\>", "Subitem",
 InitializationCell->True,
