Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " When we receive some input such as a sentence or something, then we seem \
to think consistently in some form. For instance, the raw data is infinite, \
but there are some patterns. Well, there is training data. How to build \
systems over here? In chat GPT, the input data is converted to some sort of \
embedding in a lower dimensional space where each token in the English \
language is thought of as independent from each other. That can be thought of \
as compression and indeed it works on every possible input. And what if \
receives a sequence of tokens..then it uses attention. I get it. So first \
math tokens are embedded in space so that contextual data can be applied in \
some way. Hmm. that is interesting."
}], "Item",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968925057353464*^9, 3.968925075433436*^9}, {
