6f7faabde19b"],

Cell["\<\
We can have 2 forms of raw input. English and Lean. So the processing might \
happen in both phases and we can have some sort of a compression. Let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try to take this viewpoint.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969460225874998*^9, 3.969460231372017*^9}, {
  3.96950505802994*^9, 3.969505078434408*^9}, {3.969505153316248*^9, 
  3.9695051629384604`*^9}, {3.969505969177919*^9, 3.969505970196389*^9}, {
  3.9695218303700657`*^9, 3.969521830658243*^9}, {3.96952211293929*^9, 
  3.969522113084001*^9}, {3.969522582599772*^9, 3.969522597777221*^9}, {
  3.969522964147765*^9, 3.969522996309237*^9}, {3.969523068128254*^9, 
  3.969523082169096*^9}, {3.969523240947014*^9, 3.969523287988482*^9}, {
  3.969523693683254*^9, 
  3.969523697611017*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ae31c19d-d349-45b7-95b1-\
c9ef08669e4b"],

Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s start from the first step. We want to define the \
concept of a set. And then the notion of a subset. How can we embed this? Let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try to think of this in layers where the raw input is the \
outermost layer. And then we go down when the set is considered as a \
collection of objects and make a directed arrow (or at least label it) b/c it \
is another form of representation. And then, when it subsets, it is some \
image of something being smaller so there is an edge of input node of subset, \
we go the node representing \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]something smaller\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].


 Well, that depends on the training. We will have some sort of training \
hypothesis which is the actual brain is some sort of categorisation and \
chemical reaction.  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969533044605987*^9, 3.969533059027362*^9}, {
  3.969533220243435*^9, 3.969533254230178*^9}, {3.969535281025796*^9, 
  3.969535281400365*^9}, {3.969535411054439*^9, 3.969535546054968*^9}, {
  3.96958799587062*^9, 3.969587998755911*^9}, {3.969588189280558*^9, 
  3.969588189582794*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bbcd22ed-11a2-4fd0-9fb6-\
821cb91c9048"],

Cell["\<\
For instance, if we have some region for the the definition of set and its \
examples, then where should we \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]put\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the equality of sets thing over here? Does it fall \
under \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]the concept of a set\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]? It \
doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t make sense for it to be disconnected? I guess a \
trial strategy could be where we embed these concepts as some sort of open \
sets in a topological space which allows those concepts to not be limited to \
a more rigid structure like a node. Then, equality of sets, is another \
concept that \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]intersects\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] with \
the set in some way. So le\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9695240649882936`*^9, 3.969524189082858*^9}, {
  3.969524491825591*^9, 3.969524506031351*^9}, {3.969524605318939*^9, 
  3.969524637892298*^9}, {3.96952476950915*^9, 3.9695248072013817`*^9}, {
  3.969524912984575*^9, 3.969524922076429*^9}, {3.969525023713025*^9, 
  3.969525030604241*^9}, {3.969525114927569*^9, 3.9695251193529873`*^9}, {
  3.969531509479474*^9, 3.969531636867773*^9}, {3.969533018840746*^9, 
  3.969533037368658*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7cd43ebc-e5a8-4f96-a42a-\
adf5fa6bc81e"],

Cell["\<\
So the thing is that the ideas here are just some collections of things.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969524849896276*^9, 3.969524856465904*^9}, {
  3.969524910345348*^9, 3.969524911360251*^9}, {3.969525055262043*^9, 
  3.9695250577329407`*^9}, {3.969525212915771*^9, 3.969525215592628*^9}, {
  3.969525285028872*^9, 
  3.9695253231826897`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"921d76db-be4f-472f-af34-\
01a7247716c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Well, note that may be part of what is known as the ",
 StyleBox["subconscious training which embeds...and yes...this is part. So \
this is minimizing some sort of entropy or something based on what it sees. \
seems like some physical process because they are really cool. ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969524223321711*^9, 3.969524234869149*^9}, {
  3.969524439445724*^9, 3.969524495990958*^9}, {3.969531272299955*^9, 
  3.9695312784445753`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"26139423-276a-4be7-a06e-\
8ca4f4850849"],

Cell["\<\
A first thought is what sort of a data structure we must use. The data \
structure must be flexible in the sense that if we store \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]set\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as a unit of data in the \
structure, then it can relate to many other concepts. Also, there must be \
some sort of hierarchy where we can have different layers. Now, it is about a \
certain metamathematical structure obeying some axioms. So we can just \
continue to search for it. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969523713887273*^9, 3.969523815563567*^9}, {
  3.969523876107753*^9, 3.969523877613936*^9}, {3.969523946469734*^9, 
  3.969523981130622*^9}, {3.969525122874999*^9, 
  3.969525123862*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1bb3fb4a-10b0-4349-af98-b485a9297def"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Try 1", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96968269693106*^9, 
  3.9696827040847187`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"614a58e2-b99c-4cb6-bc38-\
7fa7dc6a8a38"],

Cell["\<\
So we have a state. And then we have an action we perform. Now, the reward is \
non deterministic because we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know! I guess it is just \
a model. In the stochastic bandits, it is about learning a prob. \
distribution. So if we take some actions, we notice that some actions yield \
better results. For instance, if you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re going to a random \
cafe and you wanna try some items. Now, I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know what is \
the best item. So one strategy is to try all of them, and then decide. \
However, often every item will not be made in the exact same way. So, in \
fact, we can try each item multiple times until  we are reasonably sure about \
the average.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969871855580224*^9, 3.969871990136538*^9}, {
  3.96987206434041*^9, 3.9698720685606413`*^9}, {3.969872103416706*^9, 
  3.969872147666929*^9}, {3.969872238651857*^9, 3.969872312702429*^9}, {
  3.969872599009502*^9, 3.969872654503006*^9}, {3.969872729197267*^9, 
  3.969872755359404*^9}, {3.969872817768661*^9, 3.969872819280964*^9}, {
  3.969881935658461*^9, 
  3.969881938556664*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"67643599-de8a-444b-b558-\
56e6a533f716"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this model, we are looking at a system where our decisions ",
 StyleBox["influence ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "the system and so things become more complicated. For instance, me eating a \
cake at the cafe won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t change the cafe\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
way of making its items. However, if we are playing chess, then at each step, \
the action changes the game and so the same actions won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
have the same reward function later. We can have systems where the state \
changes in a non",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2347fde-fa68-4fc1-a533-af0c439a60b1"],
 "deterministic way."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969872757250491*^9, 3.9698727614407*^9}, {
  3.96987281464332*^9, 3.969872878711378*^9}, {3.969881956535708*^9, 
  3.9698819781990347`*^9}, {3.969882063156357*^9, 
  3.9698821161065903`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9ebc6c3b-8932-43bc-b9f9-\
d38db41c7cae"],

Cell["\<\
Gotta take a bloody course here...man. uyeah...to get gud at this shit...le\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ts think man...yeah. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969872320282922*^9, 
  3.9698723321194363`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"78c215a7-23e6-409f-9b50-\
a2ff4b389cfc"],

Cell["\<\
This is related to reinforcement larning. Hmmm....maybe all of this is \
somewhat of a markov decision process. I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know. sleepy \
as hell.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969866783721764*^9, 3.9698667858152*^9}, {
  3.969866935384167*^9, 3.96986694893297*^9}, {3.969869277357603*^9, 
  3.969869279387537*^9}, {3.9698707564389977`*^9, 3.969870759943223*^9}, {
  3.969963122357685*^9, 
  3.969963124714129*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bce1e104-c104-481d-9515-\
7f0f2a5b0d99"],

Cell["\<\
The idea here is this. When the brain receives some input like \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]set\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], it is in some region of \
the brain i.e. state. We don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t really think of it as some \
sort of a node labelled \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]set\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. \
We think of that state as some localised region of space, which is a larger \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]state space\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. And then there is \
a more abstract version consisting of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]collection of \
objects\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] inside the state space.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9696828670022306`*^9, 3.9696828880631843`*^9}, {
   3.969683060352932*^9, 3.969683107432472*^9}, {3.969683226765232*^9, 
   3.969683266014194*^9}, {3.969683332253298*^9, 3.969683374616695*^9}, {
   3.969683519936014*^9, 3.969683609733364*^9}, {3.969684045329012*^9, 
   3.969684059512103*^9}, {3.96968424585888*^9, 3.969684257476642*^9}, {
   3.9696845242818623`*^9, 3.969684526786564*^9}, {3.969684635674968*^9, 
   3.969684641698409*^9}, {3.969684813647817*^9, 3.969684824738289*^9}, {
   3.969684882566041*^9, 3.969684889809074*^9}, {3.969690269421009*^9, 
   3.969690273841218*^9}, 
   3.969690309945474*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4938b270-8a47-47e6-9995-\
0c508a38f2c2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So if there is the input: \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]a set is a collection of \
objects\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], then we might represent it by an input into \
the first layer with set being assigned a random number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "\[Element]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", "n"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"996a1e3b-b113-48cf-811d-508fece10e3c"],
 ", then collection of objects being assigned another random number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"y", "\[Element]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", "m"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"9a65ec7f-5c13-428a-9b90-c92e009b12bc"],
 " and an edge from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "->", " ", "y"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1641ab98-2729-4781-9418-4709a24db9b1"],
 ". Here we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t really care about whether ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a8e216ac-703b-4ec7-b156-a226e927c8bb"],
 " represents a set or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["y", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b8549047-f518-423d-a004-89ba05deedd0"],
 " represents a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]collection of objects\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. It just seems to be a transition from a more \
specific concept to a more hazy concept, which is a collection. The more hazy \
the concept, the more the data compression. And here we will use continuity \
constraints. Thus, the concept I need to understand is the causal structure \
of the thing, and the levels of abstraction. And the more connected things \
become, the more relative information  will be encoded."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969690310946673*^9, 3.96969032165952*^9}, {
  3.96969037574737*^9, 3.969690376862413*^9}, {3.969690441747044*^9, 
  3.969690526102462*^9}, {3.969690718964558*^9, 3.9696907478000402`*^9}, {
  3.969690863745151*^9, 3.969690909746961*^9}, {3.969690947602339*^9, 
  3.969690978653666*^9}, {3.96969121581338*^9, 3.969691237265279*^9}, {
  3.969716672780114*^9, 3.969716690263887*^9}, {3.969725572007326*^9, 
  3.9697256568259583`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"104e85d9-d0e3-4b18-9523-\
b547fe4c1d19"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And then we say a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]A subset of a set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d4df5581-b377-4311-bd70-d56525d95ca7"],
 " is a set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["B", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a347689b-6c47-41fc-a6b2-333d40926aa6"],
 " such that if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "B"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cfc9c3e-c8c3-48cd-ac04-29e4e79cd632"],
 ", then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Element]", " ", "A"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "7555beba-d1ab-4d7f-92eb-36e59418ba9d"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. So here to define element. And since we are near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "78d741ac-7b75-45a9-b97c-54f8524915f5"],
 ", we start from somewhere near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fdc124f-b63f-4eda-a322-f6c36a85dbff"],
 ", say ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "'"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b4b0d2a7-8600-402c-9659-f924f72cd2ae"],
 ", and then say that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "'"}], " ", "->", " "}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "251f8890-b645-49df-85b0-0e071a1bd224"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "'"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8245b70c-329c-461d-b275-731e91924199"],
 " is near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec04f869-f070-4c84-a9cd-37f516c48bc1"],
 " and there is a dangling edge which we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know. Then we \
explain the concept of belongs and then say that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"z", "'"}], " ", "->", " ", "z"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "59b82c8e-8f8b-4ecf-a505-6f42c0bf374b"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"z", "'"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8aa462d8-08eb-47cd-b430-78f7ca692a41"],
 " represents ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Element]", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "46ad4a08-f777-4f5e-a192-bddb571ecf1e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["z", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec144299-db15-4282-a682-67e0f4e7c47a"],
 " represents belongs i.e. an element of. Then, if we read the statement \
again (because we want to correct the uncomfortable response --- because we \
are at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "'"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d261b361-fe0c-4bbc-a303-9edc7f9b8725"],
 " i.e.. parallel processing), then we read if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbbf5733-ad34-40fa-956c-c056521b7e49"],
 " belongs to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "fd184b56-e7b3-4757-99a1-3a84af9ceebf"],
 ", then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Element]", " ", "B"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "da9047cf-4152-4d5f-88bc-b5d0ff21885a"],
 ", so we are travelling through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"z", "'"}], "->", "z"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "89e03b8c-5b8a-4360-a45f-702a13c3be62"],
 " again, strengthening the connection. And then, we say that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "'"}], " ", "->", " ", "y"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbb040c9-d72d-4dbb-9a83-a90454c24ec3"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["y", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "c116d840-9502-4700-9e03-341654917b38"],
 " represents its understanding.\n \nOkay, something like this. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969725663392727*^9, 3.969725828800605*^9}, {
   3.969725907769936*^9, 3.969726066186152*^9}, {3.969726248609934*^9, 
   3.96972635032121*^9}, {3.96972654305095*^9, 3.969726570140092*^9}, {
   3.96972683000261*^9, 3.9697268393591213`*^9}, {3.969726998295295*^9, 
   3.969727008337854*^9}, {3.969727127293448*^9, 3.969727131574815*^9}, {
   3.969755450279331*^9, 3.969755456627982*^9}, {3.969755653667657*^9, 
   3.969755654514579*^9}, {3.96975577522243*^9, 3.969755806007066*^9}, {
   3.969755853740197*^9, 3.96975586384042*^9}, {3.969755983532599*^9, 
   3.96975598455729*^9}, {3.9697560586082277`*^9, 3.969756136618013*^9}, {
   3.9697563114095583`*^9, 3.9697563238892717`*^9}, 3.969756480800591*^9, {
   3.969756628738847*^9, 
   3.969756640348825*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cef5b63c-3bb7-4662-ac93-\
dc3b5a9235eb"],

Cell["\<\
i like this idea. i THINK this can be worked out. We can read the attention \
paper to understand how things work in context.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969683112765253*^9, 3.969683189433881*^9}, 
   3.969690299348752*^9, {3.969690329835943*^9, 3.969690358284035*^9}, 
   3.969691213720751*^9, 3.96972557341934*^9, 
   3.96972590637739*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d2eed765-55ca-48f3-b85c-\
ab4363ea924e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "A weighted directed graph is a tuple ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"V", ",", "E", ",", "w"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "4449f958-f19f-4824-b30b-630ed0f39a4c"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"w", " ", ":", " ", "E"}], " ", "->", " ", 
    "\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f6f4170-96d0-4571-8bc7-61753f2f7953"],
 " are the weights assigned to edges. Here, the nodes represent conceptual \
embeddings and ideals, and the more abstract the concept, the larger the \
embedding is (compared to the space in which the thing is embedded in)."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969695179734208*^9, 3.969695256350835*^9}, {
  3.9696953112675743`*^9, 
  3.9696953446353703`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b33db7fc-2cc9-4d2e-89c3-\
6e73cbe8c417"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "A r"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969695179734208*^9, 3.969695256350835*^9}, {
  3.9696953112675743`*^9, 
  3.969695349965808*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5e80a778-6eab-4ca0-b95c-\
80f7c7215756"],

Cell["https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.08019", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.969695309480905*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d2f287ec-0a65-4187-96bf-\
b3ba5ff3cd36"],

Cell["\<\
I think whatever courses I do, it should be fine. it is easy to feel greedy \
over here. So yeah. that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s what it is is.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969683191516003*^9, 3.969683208112379*^9}, 
   3.969690549105998*^9},ExpressionUUID->"804a7927-6df4-4017-9317-\
12ac2abc609e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Second option", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9694591688706427`*^9, 
  3.969459170834165*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5d363919-d1f5-41dc-bf10-\
dfae847f4bce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s look at a bare",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fec91006-6895-4d97-9740-94a5247966fe"],
 "bones semantic representation of things . Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s start by \
looking at how alpha proof works. Yeah. Things will become much easier. So we \
can start by mapping the lean tokens to. We can start by looking at Lean \
Dojo. I think those guys have literally just done that. We can try something \
like this. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s first try to create some sort of an \
embedding over here. C"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969460245139776*^9, 3.969460261619968*^9}, {
   3.969504650767232*^9, 3.969504651640304*^9}, {3.9695049901605797`*^9, 
